    "explanation": "Rider, your dispute succeeds in full. Driver, the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee does not stand in this case.\n\nThe driver's arrival and wait are not in question. EV-TRIP-02716 records the 'arrived' event at 19:24:52 and the free waiting timer starting at 19:24:54, terminating the trip at 19:32:46 under RIDER_NO_SHOW. EV-GPS-02716 places the driver at the pickup pin (closest approach 0.0 m) for a single continuous in-geofence run of 471 seconds (19:24:52 to 19:32:43, 47 qualifying fixes). On those facts POL-NS-01 limbs (a) to (d) are met, and the arrival marker is genuine, not false, under POL-NS-05 (driver stationary at the pin, 0.0 km/h, not more than 300 m away).\n\nThe fee is nevertheless refunded in full because POL-NS-04 applies. (a) EV-CHAT-02716 shows the rider sent two locating/coordinating messages inside the waiting window: 19:25:22 ('im at the pickup, which car are you? i cant see you') and 19:27:22 ('hello? are you here'). (b) The driver posted no reply within 120 seconds of either (both read receipts are null) and trip_record.in_app_calls is empty, so no in-app voice call was placed before termination. (c) EV-GPS-02716 places the rider's device within the 150 m LARGE_VENUE rider-presence radius on all 85 qualifying fixes (mean 8.14 m, maximum 12.12 m from the pin, all at 0.0 km/h). All three limbs hold, so the rider is exonerated and the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee is refunded in full, with no driver compensation payable. POL-NS-04 is a clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06, so it displaces POL-NS-01 and the fee does not stand despite the full wait.\n\nOn the rider's POL-NS-06 argument: I do not accept that the required dwell for this zone class is 300 seconds. POL-NS-01(c) and POL-NS-06 measure against the free waiting period in force, which this record carries as platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180 s; fee_schedule.minimum_dwell_sec (300 s for LARGE_VENUE) is not applied to a record that carries platform_policy. On the correct 180 s threshold the 471 s dwell is not short, so POL-NS-06 gives no separate ground; the refund rests on POL-NS-04.\n\nOn driver compensation: POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it; POL-NS-04 displaces it here, so no compensation is payable. In any event the anti-farming check does not trip (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d 2, below the threshold of 4, and 2/58 = 0.034, below 0.08).\n\nNo escalation applies. POL-NS-09(b) is not engaged (EV-TRIP-02716 and EV-GPS-02716 agree on arrival and dwell; there is no direct contradiction), (c) is not engaged (0 counterparty disputes on both profiles), (d) is not engaged (rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d 1, below 3), and (e) is not engaged (the GPS trace is COMPLETE, 100% coverage, 10 s cadence, max gap 0.0 s, and the fare reconciles to the platform_policy figure of SGD 4.50, so there is no POL-NS-08(a)-(d) impairment). The rider's POL-NS-08 point that the trace is clean is accepted. Confidence is 0.90, above the 0.70 floor.\n\nThe traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02716-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT). It carries no fact this ruling rests on - no accumulation across separate in-geofence intervals is needed because there is only one such interval - and it does not affect the outcome. The two claims that cited it without naming its issue code were discarded by the referee under POL-GEN-02(1); that discard appears in the audit list below. The driver's statement 'I waited the full time' is consistent with the trace but does not answer the unanswered rider messages that decide this case under POL-NS-04.\n\nThe monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so this provisional ruling executes on issue. Both parties may appeal under POL-GEN-04 within 30 days."
  },
