    "explanation": "To both parties. The SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02716 is refunded to the rider in full, and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nTHE MONEY. EV-FARE-02716 (weight 1.0) carries a cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. That reconciles with the fee in force, platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd = 4.50, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) integrity defect, and the contested amount is SGD 4.50.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S CASE IS MADE OUT. POL-NS-01 is satisfied on the record: EV-TRIP-02716 carries a driver 'arrived' event at 19:24:52; EV-GPS-02716's first qualifying in-geofence fix is at the same 19:24:52 second, inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius (POL-NS-02); the continuous dwell runs 19:24:52 to 19:32:43 — 471 s, past the 180 s free waiting period in force under POL-NS-01(c) (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec); and the driver terminated at 19:32:46 under RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding event (limb (d)). POL-NS-05 is also satisfied: the arrival marker is genuine — the driver was at the pin (min distance 0.0 m, speed 0.0 kph), neither more than 300 m away nor in motion.\n\nWHY THE FEE IS NONETHELESS REFUNDED. POL-NS-04 displaces POL-NS-01, and all three of its limbs hold. (a) During the waiting window the rider sent locating/coordinating messages — 'im at the pickup, which car are you? i cant see you' at 19:25:22 and 'hello? are you here' at 19:27:22 (EV-CHAT-02716). (b) The driver posted no reply, and trip_record.in_app_calls is empty, so he neither replied within 120 seconds nor placed an in-app call before terminating. (c) The rider's device was inside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE rider-presence radius for the majority — in fact all 85 — of the qualifying fixes, mean 8.14 m and max 12.12 m from the pin. A rider who is at the pin and actively trying to coordinate, whose messages go unanswered, is exonerated: the fee is refunded in full with no driver compensation. The driver's own claims concede limbs (a) to (c), and I accept that concession.\n\nTHE RIDER'S POL-NS-06 ARGUMENT IS REJECTED. It asserts a 300-second 'minimum dwell' and a 291-second shortfall. The 300 s figure is fee_schedule.minimum_dwell_sec, which fee_schedule.resolution_rule says is retained only to interpret records authored before policy version 2 and is never applied to a record that carries platform_policy; this record carries platform_policy, and the period in force is free_wait_sec = 180 s. Nor is there a shortfall: derived.arrival.shortfall_sec of -291.0 is the 180 s minimum minus the 471 s run, i.e. a surplus of 291 s. POL-NS-06 does not fire, and the refund above follows from POL-NS-04, not from POL-NS-06.\n\nTHE MISSING ADVISORY. EV-ADVIS-02716-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT). It carries none of the deciding facts; its absence makes POL-NS-06(i) accumulation unavailable, but the driver's 471 s dwell needs no accumulation. The two claims that cited it without disclosing its issue code were discarded at Step 1 and appear in discarded_claims.\n\nNO ESCALATION AND NO REFERRAL. None of the POL-NS-09 triggers fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor; no admissible artifacts contradict each other; rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0 and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1; and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d = 2, below the 4 required, and the rate 2/58 = 0.034, below 0.08). No clause produces a referral: the arrival marker is genuine, so POL-NS-05(ii) does not fire, and POL-NS-01's driver-education referral arises only where the reason code was mis-selected, whereas RIDER_NO_SHOW is one of the three codes limb (d) recognises. Because POL-NS-04 displaces POL-NS-01, no driver compensation is payable even though POL-NS-07's anti-farming test would otherwise have permitted it (EV-DPROF-02716, weight 1.0).\n\nCONFIDENCE AND EXECUTION. Confidence 0.9. The deciding facts are carried by EV-CHAT-02716, EV-TRIP-02716 and EV-GPS-02716, each at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. The monetary effect, SGD 4.50, is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so it executes automatically; this ruling is provisional and either party may appeal once under POL-GEN-04."
